235
00:11:17,468 --> 00:11:21,222
Okay, but, like, seriously?
Oh, man, for real?

236
00:11:23,265 --> 00:11:28,437
Well, you know, from the time that
I was in second grade to sixth grade,

237
00:11:28,521 --> 00:11:29,980
I was, like, abused.

238
00:11:30,606 --> 00:11:34,443
And when I entered
junior high school, I had no outlet,

239
00:11:34,527 --> 00:11:37,238
nowhere to put everything
that I was feeling.

240
00:11:37,321 --> 00:11:40,741
And so,
I was pretty intense during that time.

241
00:11:40,825 --> 00:11:43,160
Once I lost my temper,
I couldn't stop myself.

242
00:11:43,244 --> 00:11:44,245
I'm still like that.

243
00:11:44,328 --> 00:11:48,040
And so, like, with my younger brother,

244
00:11:48,124 --> 00:11:50,418
honestly, I used to hit him and stuff.

245
00:11:51,210 --> 00:11:54,130
I took my feelings out on other people,
on my mom, even.

246
00:11:55,548 --> 00:11:57,133
To be honest…

247
00:11:57,216 --> 00:12:02,054
me and my younger brother don't talk
to each other at all anymore.

248
00:12:05,099 --> 00:12:08,060
My younger brother saw how I was,
and he said,

249
00:12:08,144 --> 00:12:10,396
"I don't want anything to do with you.

250
00:12:10,479 --> 00:12:12,982
I don't want people knowing
you're my sister.

251
00:12:13,065 --> 00:12:14,316
So, just stay away from me."

252
00:12:16,652 --> 00:12:19,822
And, you know, my room was
sort of a hangout spot for friends

253
00:12:19,905 --> 00:12:21,574
when I was in junior high.

254
00:12:21,657 --> 00:12:23,868
Like, my whole house was, actually.

255
00:12:24,410 --> 00:12:26,871
We would drink, we would smoke,

256
00:12:26,954 --> 00:12:29,373
and there were always guys coming over.

257
00:12:29,457 --> 00:12:33,002
My younger brother
probably saw a lot of that.

258
00:12:33,544 --> 00:12:35,421
So, he told me that

259
00:12:36,255 --> 00:12:38,132
he didn't see me as his sister.

260
00:12:39,842 --> 00:12:44,597
It was hard for me, of course,
but I thought, "Well, I can't blame him."

261
00:12:46,098 --> 00:12:47,767
The police came to our house a lot,

262
00:12:47,850 --> 00:12:50,728
because I would throw
these super violent tantrums.

263
00:12:52,104 --> 00:12:54,231
So, he saw all of those things,

264
00:12:54,315 --> 00:12:56,692
and naturally, my brother felt scared.

265
00:12:57,902 --> 00:13:00,780
At least,
it seems like he was scared of me.

266
00:13:01,864 --> 00:13:04,742
My whole family rides motorcycles.
Everyone.

267
00:13:04,825 --> 00:13:09,121
But my younger brother refuses
to ride one, no matter what.

268
00:13:09,205 --> 00:13:11,081
And, you know, I think it's because of me.

269
00:13:11,749 --> 00:13:15,085
I think it's because he doesn't want

270
00:13:15,669 --> 00:13:17,713
to be like his sister, in any way.

271
00:13:19,882 --> 00:13:21,550
He told me to stay away,

272
00:13:22,593 --> 00:13:23,886
to never speak to him.

273
00:13:25,346 --> 00:13:27,223
I think I…

274
00:13:29,183 --> 00:13:33,395
honestly, did something really terrible
to my younger brother.

275
00:13:35,815 --> 00:13:39,735
When I started to go off the rails,
my younger sister was still very young.

276
00:13:40,319 --> 00:13:43,531
I'd have some friends over,
friends I used to do bad things with.

277
00:13:43,614 --> 00:13:46,367
I didn't think anything of it
at the time, though.

278
00:13:46,450 --> 00:13:48,285
But when I asked her about it later,

279
00:13:48,369 --> 00:13:51,372
she told me that
those guys scared her a lot.

280
00:13:51,997 --> 00:13:54,208
But I was only thinking
about having fun at the time.

281
00:13:54,291 --> 00:13:56,252
I didn't think about her at all.

282
00:13:56,335 --> 00:13:59,672
But now I'm older,
and I've thought about it more.

283
00:13:59,755 --> 00:14:02,633
And I feel bad for scaring her like that.

284
00:14:03,425 --> 00:14:06,929
My sister's life is the total opposite.
She studied super hard.

285
00:14:07,763 --> 00:14:09,265
- Mmm.
- Mmm.

286
00:14:09,348 --> 00:14:11,809
My younger sister's the same.
She studies a lot.

287
00:14:11,892 --> 00:14:13,686
But my last name is unusual,

288
00:14:13,769 --> 00:14:16,063
so the teachers at school
remember it easily.

289
00:14:16,146 --> 00:14:17,731
- I had that too.
- Yeah.

290
00:14:18,232 --> 00:14:21,193
My last name is Sagae. They'd say,
"That's Sagae's younger sister."

291
00:14:21,277 --> 00:14:22,528
- Yeah.
- Mmm-hmm.

292
00:14:22,611 --> 00:14:24,822
But, honestly,
she's not like me in any way.

293
00:14:24,905 --> 00:14:25,990
She's very serious.

294
00:14:26,532 --> 00:14:29,493
She studied hard
and got a university scholarship.

295
00:14:29,577 --> 00:14:30,828
- Amazing.
- Wow.

296
00:14:30,911 --> 00:14:34,582
Yeah. She did everything she could
to avoid causing trouble for our parents.

297
00:14:35,291 --> 00:14:37,501
I was the oldest son,
but so irresponsible.

298
00:14:38,794 --> 00:14:43,424
When I grew up and got a job, I thought
I should get my act together.

299
00:14:43,507 --> 00:14:45,968
Maybe you could call him
and ask him to dinner.

300
00:14:46,051 --> 00:14:48,596
- Right.
- And talk it out with him.

301
00:14:48,679 --> 00:14:50,097
Even if it's embarrassing.

302
00:14:50,681 --> 00:14:53,058
I mean, you're siblings,
so you should definitely talk.

303
00:14:53,142 --> 00:14:55,811
- Express your gratitude to him directly.
- Right.

304
00:14:55,895 --> 00:14:57,563
I haven't been able to say that

305
00:14:57,646 --> 00:15:00,107
- to my sister. It's hard.
- Yeah, I haven't either.

306
00:15:00,774 --> 00:15:01,942
It's kind of embarrassing--

307
00:15:02,026 --> 00:15:03,986
You should be able to trust your family.

308
00:15:04,069 --> 00:15:05,195
Yeah.

309
00:15:05,279 --> 00:15:07,573
- It's a bond that can't be broken.
- Yeah.

310
00:15:08,324 --> 00:15:12,703
And like, also,
I've been pregnant twice in my life.

311
00:15:14,163 --> 00:15:15,205
Yeah.

312
00:15:16,165 --> 00:15:17,875
The first time, I was 18.

313
00:15:17,958 --> 00:15:21,712
And then, the second time I got pregnant,
I was 22 years old.

314
00:15:22,630 --> 00:15:23,881
Yeah, but like…

315
00:15:24,798 --> 00:15:27,384
they don't exist anymore, you know?

316
00:15:28,761 --> 00:15:30,179
I don't know how else to say it.

317
00:15:30,262 --> 00:15:35,142
But, back then, there was someone
I honestly wanted to be with forever.

318
00:15:37,019 --> 00:15:39,271
And I got pregnant with his baby.

319
00:15:39,897 --> 00:15:43,275
But at that time, like, when I was 18,

320
00:15:44,068 --> 00:15:47,613
I wasn't taking life too seriously,
and I didn't have any money.

321
00:15:47,696 --> 00:15:50,407
And, you know, the guy had his own issues.

322
00:15:51,283 --> 00:15:55,704
But I still wanted to have the baby,
even if it meant I had to be a single mom.

323
00:15:57,665 --> 00:15:59,541
But I decided to get an abortion.

324
00:15:59,625 --> 00:16:02,294
And so, I had the surgery,

325
00:16:02,378 --> 00:16:05,839
and when I finally woke up
from the anesthesia…

326
00:16:05,923 --> 00:16:08,342
…I could really tell that
the baby wasn't in my belly.

327
00:16:09,009 --> 00:16:11,220
How should I put it?

328
00:16:11,303 --> 00:16:13,764
It was like that part of me
was completely empty.

329
00:16:17,768 --> 00:16:18,936
That's how it felt.

330
00:16:20,312 --> 00:16:23,399
I was like, "Oh, okay.
It's just gone now."

331
00:16:27,152 --> 00:16:32,199
That was so hard for me. And, like,
I want to apologize to that baby.

332
00:16:32,825 --> 00:16:36,286
Yeah, but it doesn't exist anymore,

333
00:16:36,370 --> 00:16:37,871
so maybe there's that too.

334
00:16:39,331 --> 00:16:40,332
Mmm.

335
00:16:42,751 --> 00:16:45,337
You know, I actually had an abortion too.

336
00:16:45,879 --> 00:16:49,425
I was… maybe 16 years old, I think?

337
00:16:50,217 --> 00:16:54,221
I was living with my boyfriend
at the time, and I got pregnant.

338
00:16:55,639 --> 00:16:58,851
At the time, I thought of myself
as very independent.

339
00:16:59,435 --> 00:17:03,480
I went to the hospital, but I needed
my parents' permission to have the baby.

340
00:17:04,106 --> 00:17:05,941
And they were totally against it.

341
00:17:08,152 --> 00:17:09,403
So…

342
00:17:12,072 --> 00:17:13,991
we fought a lot about
whether I should have it.

343
00:17:15,325 --> 00:17:18,662
And I ended up having an abortion,
a major surgery.

344
00:17:18,746 --> 00:17:22,416
There was this overwhelming sense
that it was gone, you know?

345
00:17:23,834 --> 00:17:27,337
Waking up from anesthesia,
and feeling that it's gone,

346
00:17:27,421 --> 00:17:28,380
I remembered that…

347
00:17:28,881 --> 00:17:30,340
so vividly just now.

348
00:17:32,593 --> 00:17:34,928
And then, that became part of my life,

349
00:17:35,429 --> 00:17:38,140
it's part of my experience,
and who I am now.

350
00:17:39,433 --> 00:17:42,061
Of course, it didn't end the way
I wanted it to, but,

351
00:17:43,145 --> 00:17:46,065
I want to keep that experience
close to my heart.

352
00:17:46,148 --> 00:17:48,942
That's what I was thinking,
listening to your story.

353
00:17:49,026 --> 00:17:50,152
Mmm.

354
00:17:52,529 --> 00:17:53,447
Mmm.

355
00:17:58,327 --> 00:18:00,662
- Everyone's stories were so deep.
- Mmm.

356
00:18:00,746 --> 00:18:02,456
- They hit me hard.
- Yeah.

357
00:18:02,539 --> 00:18:06,293
This kind of deep conversation,
or a chance to talk about your past,

358
00:18:06,376 --> 00:18:08,754
- doesn't happen very often, right?
- No, it doesn't.

359
00:18:09,588 --> 00:18:12,758
But I realized that it's important
to have an opportunity to do that.

360
00:18:12,841 --> 00:18:15,677
- Right.
- Yeah. But I feel so embarrassed about it.

361
00:18:15,761 --> 00:18:16,595
Yeah.

362
00:18:16,678 --> 00:18:20,390
Like, I don't even talk to my brother
or my parents about it.

363
00:18:20,474 --> 00:18:23,102
I don't think you need
to be embarrassed at all.

364
00:18:24,394 --> 00:18:25,312
I think…

365
00:18:26,522 --> 00:18:29,900
your story resonated with everyone.
It reminded me that

366
00:18:30,484 --> 00:18:33,403
I'll want to cherish my child
if I ever have one.

367
00:18:35,072 --> 00:18:36,990
- We all felt it.
- Yeah.

368
00:18:37,783 --> 00:18:38,826
Mmm.

369
00:18:42,704 --> 00:18:46,875
I was like, "I want to have the baby."
But I got pregnant by a married man.

370
00:18:46,959 --> 00:18:48,877
- <i>I see.</i>
- Yeah, he had a wife.

371
00:18:49,795 --> 00:18:50,629
So…

372
00:18:51,880 --> 00:18:54,174
I cried so hard. Then I got an abortion.

373
00:19:00,597 --> 00:19:04,184
SHOW YOUR RESOLVE

374
00:19:15,612 --> 00:19:16,488
I'm nervous.

375
00:19:35,382 --> 00:19:37,009
- <i>Hello?</i>
- Hey there.

376
00:19:37,092 --> 00:19:38,552
<i>What's going on?</i>

377
00:19:39,178 --> 00:19:40,304
Nothing, really.

378
00:19:41,096 --> 00:19:42,264
I just…

379
00:19:42,347 --> 00:19:44,641
- <i>Yeah?</i>
- <i>Is this her mom?</i>

380
00:19:44,725 --> 00:19:45,934
- <i>Yes.</i>
- <i>Oh.</i>

381
00:19:46,602 --> 00:19:49,354
Like, when I was
still in junior high school…

382
00:19:49,438 --> 00:19:50,480
<i>Yeah?</i>

383
00:19:50,564 --> 00:19:52,191
…I was a bit rebellious, you know?

384
00:19:53,400 --> 00:19:54,484
<i>Yeah.</i>

385
00:19:55,319 --> 00:19:59,323
And, I mean, I never took
the chance to apologize to you

386
00:19:59,406 --> 00:20:00,657
for all of that, so.

387
00:20:01,491 --> 00:20:05,120
<i>Oh, come on.</i>
<i>That's all in the past. Forget about it.</i>

388
00:20:06,371 --> 00:20:09,374
Sure, but, there's something else
I haven't told you.

389
00:20:09,458 --> 00:20:11,293
- <i>What?</i>
- I couldn't, till now.

390
00:20:11,919 --> 00:20:12,920
Uh…

391
00:20:14,046 --> 00:20:16,965
I haven't told you
for about two years, but…

392
00:20:17,049 --> 00:20:18,342
<i>Yeah?</i>

393
00:20:18,425 --> 00:20:21,511
…I got pregnant with my second child.

394
00:20:22,179 --> 00:20:23,680
- <i>What?</i>
- Yeah.

395
00:20:23,764 --> 00:20:27,142
Mmm… Yeah, when I was 22.

396
00:20:28,685 --> 00:20:31,730
But, of course,
I never told you about that, so…

397
00:20:33,273 --> 00:20:35,359
I wanted to tell you now.

398
00:20:37,319 --> 00:20:38,695
<i>Ah.</i>

399
00:20:42,658 --> 00:20:43,659
<i>Well…</i>

400
00:20:46,286 --> 00:20:48,121
<i>don't let that happen again.</i>

401
00:20:48,205 --> 00:20:49,039
Mmm.

402
00:20:49,122 --> 00:20:51,667
- <i>I mean, it's a life.</i>
- Mmm.

403
00:20:54,544 --> 00:20:57,589
<i>In the end, that child has no say in that.</i>

404
00:20:57,673 --> 00:20:58,507
Right.

405
00:20:59,633 --> 00:21:00,759
<i>Yeah.</i>

406
00:21:03,887 --> 00:21:06,431
<i>- Life is extremely precious.</i>
- Mmm.

407
00:21:06,515 --> 00:21:08,433
<i>You should think about that.</i>

408
00:21:08,517 --> 00:21:09,476
Mmm.

409
00:21:11,311 --> 00:21:13,438
<i>How long did you carry for?</i>

410
00:21:13,522 --> 00:21:15,274
<i>Do you have an ultrasound photo?</i>

411
00:21:15,357 --> 00:21:17,567
I do. It's on my wall at home.

412
00:21:19,903 --> 00:21:23,073
<i>When I was pregnant</i>
<i>with you, Ayana, and your brother…</i>

413
00:21:23,156 --> 00:21:25,409
- Yeah?
- <i>…for both of you…</i>

414
00:21:25,492 --> 00:21:27,077
- Mmm.
- <i>I was told that</i>

415
00:21:27,160 --> 00:21:29,997
<i>I might not be able</i>
<i>to carry you to term, but I did.</i>

416
00:21:30,080 --> 00:21:30,914
Right.

417
00:21:33,041 --> 00:21:34,293
<i>Firstly,</i>

418
00:21:34,960 --> 00:21:36,795
<i>parents protect their kids.</i>

419
00:21:37,421 --> 00:21:38,380
Mmm.

420
00:21:38,964 --> 00:21:42,467
<i>No matter how far</i>
<i>they stray, or the trouble they have.</i>

421
00:21:43,510 --> 00:21:46,847
<i>I would have risked my life</i>
<i>to protect you two.</i>

422
00:21:47,806 --> 00:21:50,475
<i>That's honestly</i>
<i>all I could think at that time.</i>

423
00:21:50,559 --> 00:21:51,393
Mmm.

424
00:21:52,644 --> 00:21:54,479
<i>That's what raising kids is.</i>

425
00:21:54,980 --> 00:21:56,481
- Right.
- <i>Yeah?</i>

426
00:22:00,652 --> 00:22:03,030
<i>I mean, nothing can be done about it now.</i>

427
00:22:05,532 --> 00:22:08,744
But, you know,
I think I've said to you before, that…

428
00:22:09,953 --> 00:22:13,457
I wish I hadn't been born to you
and that you weren't my mother.

429
00:22:14,166 --> 00:22:15,292
<i>Yeah.</i>

430
00:22:19,004 --> 00:22:21,548
Yeah. I wanted to apologize for that too.

431
00:22:22,758 --> 00:22:23,842
I'm so sorry.

432
00:22:29,514 --> 00:22:31,224
<i>Well, you know,</i>

433
00:22:32,142 --> 00:22:35,520
<i>whether it's something you regret</i>
<i>or something you feel good about,</i>

434
00:22:35,604 --> 00:22:37,898
<i>the present only exists</i>
<i>because of the past.</i>

435
00:22:37,981 --> 00:22:39,483
- Mmm.
- <i>Yeah.</i>

436
00:22:40,067 --> 00:22:42,861
<i>So, there's no need to apologize at all.</i>

437
00:22:44,071 --> 00:22:44,946
Mmm.

438
00:22:47,032 --> 00:22:49,409
<i>I'm still learning every day, as well.</i>

439
00:22:49,493 --> 00:22:50,327
Right.

440
00:22:50,827 --> 00:22:52,996
<i>I still make mistakes.</i>

441
00:22:53,080 --> 00:22:56,041
<i>And there are times when I think,</i>
<i>"Oh, I'm glad I did that."</i>

442
00:22:56,124 --> 00:22:58,043
<i>That's how everyone grows in life.</i>

443
00:22:58,126 --> 00:22:59,795
- Mmm.
- <i>Yeah.</i>

444
00:22:59,878 --> 00:23:03,382
<i>You know, a parent would</i>
<i>never abandon their child.</i>

445
00:23:04,049 --> 00:23:04,883
Yeah.

446
00:23:08,428 --> 00:23:10,472
But, like, thank you
for giving birth to me.

447
00:23:10,972 --> 00:23:12,682
<i>Sure.</i>

448
00:23:17,562 --> 00:23:19,689
<i>- You've got a long life ahead.</i>
- Thank you.

449
00:23:20,232 --> 00:23:21,691
- <i>Of course.</i>
- Bye.

450
00:23:37,416 --> 00:23:40,335
- She told the class her story.
- Oh, wow.

451
00:23:40,419 --> 00:23:42,712
Ayacheru opened up
and shared her past with everyone.

452
00:23:42,796 --> 00:23:43,797
- Mmm-hmm.
- Right?

453
00:23:43,880 --> 00:23:44,965
Mmm.

454
00:23:45,048 --> 00:23:46,299
I chose to get

455
00:23:46,967 --> 00:23:48,760
- an abortion too, at one point.
- Oh.

456
00:23:48,844 --> 00:23:52,347
It was during a time that my husband
was in and out of prison.

457
00:23:52,431 --> 00:23:55,183
- I didn't think that I could do it.
- I see.

458
00:23:55,267 --> 00:23:57,686
So ultimately,
I decided not to have the baby.

459
00:23:57,769 --> 00:24:01,148
It's such a physical burden,
and mentally, of course.

460
00:24:01,231 --> 00:24:02,065
Mm.

461
00:24:02,149 --> 00:24:04,901
You know, men also bear
a burden in that situation,

462
00:24:04,985 --> 00:24:07,446
and they may provide financial support,

463
00:24:07,529 --> 00:24:11,074
and some men may provide
emotional support, as well.

464
00:24:11,158 --> 00:24:11,992
Sure.

465
00:24:12,075 --> 00:24:14,661
But it's the women
who physically experience it.

466
00:24:14,744 --> 00:24:15,912
- Right.
- Mmm-hmm.

467
00:24:15,996 --> 00:24:20,292
Even when they make the decision together,
a woman still ends up blaming herself.

468
00:24:20,375 --> 00:24:23,044
That's why I think that
women need to try and be…

469
00:24:23,753 --> 00:24:26,673
twice as careful as men,
in their relationships.

470
00:24:27,674 --> 00:24:29,634
I think this Ethics class
is so good for them.

471
00:24:29,718 --> 00:24:31,595
- Isn't it?
- More places should offer it.

472
00:24:31,678 --> 00:24:32,512
Yeah.

473
00:24:32,596 --> 00:24:35,932
You know, people usually try to look cool
when they're looking for partners.

474
00:24:36,016 --> 00:24:39,352
But if you start by fully
opening yourself up, it helps so much.

475
00:24:39,436 --> 00:24:41,980
- It takes courage. Because, you think…
- Absolutely.

476
00:24:42,063 --> 00:24:45,108
…"How am I supposed to find
a romantic partner from here?

477
00:24:45,192 --> 00:24:47,527
- From such a vulnerable place?"
- You're so right.

478
00:24:47,611 --> 00:24:49,446
But you can. That's what…

479
00:24:50,322 --> 00:24:52,199
this show is ultimately trying
to prove, right?

480
00:24:52,282 --> 00:24:54,951
- Whoa. That's so wise.
- Thank you. You're so right.

481
00:24:55,035 --> 00:24:56,203
- Yeah.
- Exactly.

482
00:24:59,748 --> 00:25:03,210
<i>Today, you will be helping out Ms. Higa,</i>

483
00:25:03,293 --> 00:25:04,961
<i>who runs an orchard.</i>

484
00:25:05,754 --> 00:25:09,299
<i>Please give it your all,</i>
<i>and help her as much as you can.</i>

485
00:25:10,634 --> 00:25:11,927
- Hello.
- Been a while.

486
00:25:12,010 --> 00:25:13,136
Yes.

487
00:25:13,845 --> 00:25:15,347
- Remember me?
- Welcome. I remember.

488
00:25:15,430 --> 00:25:16,765
- You're back so soon.
- I flunked.

489
00:25:16,848 --> 00:25:17,682
MS. HIGA

490
00:25:17,766 --> 00:25:19,726
- That's fine. Keep trying.
- I'll keep trying.

491
00:25:19,809 --> 00:25:21,228
- Nice to meet you.
- Hello.

492
00:25:21,311 --> 00:25:23,438
- The ladies are always so beautiful.
- Oh, really?

493
00:25:23,522 --> 00:25:25,106
Every time.

494
00:25:25,190 --> 00:25:26,566
- It's the truth.
- Nice to meet you.

495
00:25:26,650 --> 00:25:30,946
This building was already pretty old
when I decided to buy it,

496
00:25:31,780 --> 00:25:33,782
about 45 years ago

497
00:25:33,865 --> 00:25:35,992
- I see.
- I held church here for a while.

498
00:25:36,076 --> 00:25:37,619
I was running a service.

499
00:25:37,702 --> 00:25:39,621
But the number of people
has decreased so much

500
00:25:39,704 --> 00:25:42,791
that now we go to another place
and worship together there instead.

501
00:25:42,874 --> 00:25:46,127
Sometimes, there are people
who come and stay the night.

502
00:25:46,211 --> 00:25:49,130
People who do gymnastics ask
to use it sometimes.

503
00:25:49,214 --> 00:25:51,466
So, that's what happens here now.

504
00:25:51,550 --> 00:25:53,885
As you set out to clean this place,

505
00:25:53,969 --> 00:25:57,013
I'd be grateful if you cleaned
with the utmost care.

506
00:25:57,097 --> 00:25:58,682
- Please be careful.
- Understood.

507
00:25:58,765 --> 00:26:00,183
- Yes, thank you.
- Leave it to us.

508
00:26:01,476 --> 00:26:03,937
- Let's start with the floor.
- Yeah.

509
00:26:04,020 --> 00:26:05,313
- Ready?
- Ready.

510
00:26:05,397 --> 00:26:06,356
And, go!

511
00:26:06,439 --> 00:26:07,607
Wait, I can't.

512
00:26:12,153 --> 00:26:13,071
Let's go.

513
00:26:14,698 --> 00:26:15,782
Doing good!

514
00:26:17,075 --> 00:26:18,618
Nice, nice, good work.

515
00:26:19,661 --> 00:26:22,289
- <i>Doing it right.</i>
- <i>Cleaning properly. Wonderful.</i>

516
00:26:22,372 --> 00:26:23,999
- There!
- That's insane.

517
00:26:24,082 --> 00:26:25,166
I'm tired.

518
00:26:25,250 --> 00:26:27,877
- It's pretty hard work.
- Yeah, you're right.

519
00:26:31,673 --> 00:26:33,967
- Does the floor look clean?
- What'd you think?

520
00:26:34,050 --> 00:26:35,969
- Oh, thank you so much!
- It's sparkling.

521
00:26:36,553 --> 00:26:37,929
- Truly!
- Of course.

522
00:26:38,013 --> 00:26:40,473
On Saturday,
about 20 people will stay here.

523
00:26:40,557 --> 00:26:41,391
Okay.

524
00:26:41,474 --> 00:26:43,685
They'll be children and teachers
from a nursery school.

525
00:26:43,768 --> 00:26:45,395
- Oh, yeah?
- Thank you for coming.

526
00:26:45,478 --> 00:26:48,231
- Your timing is perfect.
- Of course. Our pleasure.

527
00:26:48,315 --> 00:26:50,734
Actually, this here

528
00:26:50,817 --> 00:26:53,778
was made a while back
by the leader of the church.

529
00:26:53,862 --> 00:26:54,904
THE CLOCK OF LIFE

530
00:26:54,988 --> 00:26:57,490
This is such a great piece
of advice, for anyone.

531
00:26:58,074 --> 00:27:00,076
- Let's all read it together, okay?
- Okay.

532
00:27:00,160 --> 00:27:01,036
All right.

533
00:27:01,119 --> 00:27:06,207
"The clock of life is wound but once."

534
00:27:06,916 --> 00:27:10,211
"When the hands will come to a stop,

535
00:27:10,295 --> 00:27:12,005
whether it's later,

536
00:27:12,088 --> 00:27:14,382
- or much sooner in life…
- Louder, everyone.

537
00:27:14,466 --> 00:27:16,509
…no one can know."

538
00:27:16,593 --> 00:27:20,221
"The present is the only time you own."

539
00:27:20,847 --> 00:27:26,394
"Live. Love.
And be sure to labor with all your heart."

540
00:27:27,270 --> 00:27:31,149
"You must not count on tomorrow,

541
00:27:31,232 --> 00:27:34,235
because tomorrow,

542
00:27:34,319 --> 00:27:38,948
your clock of life
may have stopped ticking."

543
00:27:39,491 --> 00:27:43,078
This is a very thought-provoking quote.
It's good to keep in mind.

544
00:27:43,161 --> 00:27:45,372
You only live once, that's for sure.

545
00:27:45,455 --> 00:27:47,332
- So live in the moment.
- Exactly!

546
00:27:47,415 --> 00:27:50,251
- Do your best in the moment.
- Appreciate the present, right?

547
00:27:50,335 --> 00:27:52,962
You all have a long life ahead of you,

548
00:27:53,046 --> 00:27:55,965
so live for now,
and do your best in your life.

549
00:27:56,049 --> 00:27:57,592
Don't waste your time, okay?

550
00:27:57,676 --> 00:28:00,053
I will live in the moment
and focus on the present.

551
00:28:00,136 --> 00:28:01,930
- Yes, right.
- Thanks so much.

552
00:28:02,013 --> 00:28:03,682
Thank you for everything.

553
00:28:04,516 --> 00:28:05,558
RYOPI (29)
BAR OWNER

554
00:28:05,642 --> 00:28:08,645
The clock of life.
Yeah, it was good. Live in the moment.

555
00:28:09,854 --> 00:28:12,065
I feel like my mind is so clear now.

556
00:28:13,566 --> 00:28:14,943
It felt so good.

557
00:28:16,069 --> 00:28:19,447
The things you choose to do,
ultimately define you, after all.

558
00:28:20,156 --> 00:28:22,575
Now, I want to know more about myself

559
00:28:22,659 --> 00:28:25,495
about what I might be lacking,
and stuff like that.

560
00:28:27,122 --> 00:28:29,499
- Does Ms. Higa live alone?
- Must be lonely.

561
00:28:29,582 --> 00:28:32,085
Well, there are
some kids with disabilities living there.

562
00:28:32,168 --> 00:28:33,044
Mmm.

563
00:28:33,128 --> 00:28:35,255
Yeah, and there are children
without any relatives

564
00:28:35,338 --> 00:28:36,548
who also stay there with her.

565
00:28:36,631 --> 00:28:37,549
Okay.

566
00:28:37,632 --> 00:28:40,760
Ms. Higa wanted us from part one
to spend time playing with the kids,

567
00:28:40,844 --> 00:28:43,179
- if we had an opportunity to go back.
- Wonderful.

568
00:28:43,263 --> 00:28:45,765
But that didn't happen.
Not for me, at least.

569
00:28:45,849 --> 00:28:48,727
Oh, I see. I want to go back
and help clean again.

570
00:28:48,810 --> 00:28:49,644
Same.

571
00:28:49,728 --> 00:28:51,479
I want to give them something
they can keep.

572
00:28:51,563 --> 00:28:52,897
- For sure.
- Like a gift.

573
00:28:52,981 --> 00:28:55,483
- What should we bring?
- Or something else we could do.

574
00:28:55,567 --> 00:28:57,944
<i>It turned into</i>
<i>a wholesome brainstorming session.</i>

575
00:28:58,027 --> 00:29:00,864
- What can we do?
- I wonder what would make them happy.

576
00:29:00,947 --> 00:29:01,781
Hmm.

577
00:29:01,865 --> 00:29:03,867
If the kids are happy,
Ms. Higa will be happy.

578
00:29:03,950 --> 00:29:04,951
- Right.
- True.

579
00:29:05,493 --> 00:29:07,746
- I wonder if we can make a bench.
- Oh! Okay.

580
00:29:07,829 --> 00:29:09,539
- That's a good idea.
- That's nice.

581
00:29:09,622 --> 00:29:12,000
Yeah, we could make something together,
like a bench.

582
00:29:12,083 --> 00:29:14,085
- And they can look at the view.
- Great idea!

583
00:29:14,169 --> 00:29:15,962
- Awesome idea.
- The best!

584
00:29:16,045 --> 00:29:18,006
- Sound good?
- Yeah! You're smart.

585
00:29:18,089 --> 00:29:19,090
- Perfect.
- Awesome.

586
00:29:19,174 --> 00:29:20,383
Stop, you're flattering me.

587
00:29:20,467 --> 00:29:22,427
- Wasn't talking to you.
- Don't take credit.

588
00:29:22,510 --> 00:29:25,013
I wasn't talking to you.

589
00:29:30,143 --> 00:29:32,228
What's the longest relationship
you've been in?

590
00:29:32,312 --> 00:29:34,272
- Five years.
- That's long! For real?

591
00:29:34,355 --> 00:29:35,648
Maybe about six years.

592
00:29:35,732 --> 00:29:37,025
- That's crazy.
- Five or six.

593
00:29:37,108 --> 00:29:39,360
- I see.
- I thought I was gonna marry her.

594
00:29:39,444 --> 00:29:41,821
- Wow, well, naturally.
- Yeah.

595
00:29:41,905 --> 00:29:44,449
- That's when I was working construction.
- Why did you break up?

596
00:29:44,532 --> 00:29:46,451
- Well, she was super pretty.
- Mmm.

597
00:29:47,494 --> 00:29:49,829
So a lot of guys around me
were super jealous of me.

598
00:29:49,913 --> 00:29:53,416
And they'd tell her they saw me out
with another girl, stuff like that.

599
00:29:53,917 --> 00:29:55,043
It was too much.

600
00:29:55,126 --> 00:29:57,295
- Oh, really?
- It happened a lot.

601
00:29:58,171 --> 00:29:59,839
There were rumors with my ex too.

602
00:30:00,381 --> 00:30:04,385
He cheated on me, like, six times,
and with the same girl.

603
00:30:05,428 --> 00:30:07,597
- They'd started as friends with benefits.
- I see.

604
00:30:08,389 --> 00:30:10,475
And I told him, "I'll kill you."

605
00:30:10,558 --> 00:30:11,559
Kill him?

606
00:30:11,643 --> 00:30:13,770
But I loved him too much,
so I forgave him.

607
00:30:13,853 --> 00:30:16,481
So, yeah,
I haven't had a good relationship.

608
00:30:17,106 --> 00:30:18,107
How many have you had?

609
00:30:18,191 --> 00:30:19,275
- Ex-boyfriends?
- Exes, yeah.

610
00:30:19,359 --> 00:30:21,903
- Just two.
- Two, huh? Same for me.

611
00:30:22,487 --> 00:30:24,572
- You're lying. For real?
- No, I'm serious. Yeah.

612
00:30:24,656 --> 00:30:26,741
Well, you were taken for five years.

613
00:30:26,825 --> 00:30:28,993
- I started the bar after that.
- Oh, I see.

614
00:30:29,077 --> 00:30:31,579
I've been running it for six years,
and I've been too busy.

615
00:30:31,663 --> 00:30:32,789
A long time.

616
00:30:32,872 --> 00:30:34,040
What's your blood type?

617
00:30:35,250 --> 00:30:37,168
Worn-out type.

618
00:30:37,252 --> 00:30:39,420
I'm just playing. It's B. I'm so sorry.

619
00:30:39,504 --> 00:30:41,714
- My apologies.
- You're a B?

620
00:30:41,798 --> 00:30:43,716
Oh, I see.

621
00:30:43,800 --> 00:30:46,511
- And you? O?
- I can only get along with B.

622
00:30:46,594 --> 00:30:48,054
- What? You're O.
- Nope.

623
00:30:48,137 --> 00:30:50,306
- What is it then?
- People are usually put off.

624
00:30:50,390 --> 00:30:52,308
- Are you A type?
- People are so put off by it.

625
00:30:52,392 --> 00:30:54,060
- Come on, tell me.
- It's frigid.

626
00:30:54,143 --> 00:30:55,728
No way!

627
00:30:57,480 --> 00:30:59,649
- <i>They're having fun.</i>
- <i>Looks fun.</i>

628
00:30:59,732 --> 00:31:02,151
- So, what's your blood type?
- AB.

629
00:31:02,235 --> 00:31:03,319
- You're an AB?
- Yeah.

630
00:31:03,403 --> 00:31:04,320
I see.

631
00:31:04,404 --> 00:31:07,282
But all of my exes had
the same type, they were also B.

632
00:31:11,119 --> 00:31:13,663
- It feels like we shouldn't be watching.
- Yes.

633
00:31:13,746 --> 00:31:15,456
They're being so lovey-dovey.

634
00:31:15,540 --> 00:31:18,668
They're having
such a lively, silly conversation.

635
00:31:18,751 --> 00:31:22,255
- Can only happen if they like each other.
- So, they might be the miracle couple.

636
00:31:22,839 --> 00:31:24,382
- Both born on this planet.
- Exactly!

637
00:31:24,465 --> 00:31:27,051
- They are a good match.
- Might be a miracle.

638
00:31:30,638 --> 00:31:32,932
- The girls.
- Hey there.

639
00:31:33,016 --> 00:31:34,976
- Good morning, everyone.
- Morning.

640
00:31:35,059 --> 00:31:37,395
Good morning. Good morning, everyone.

641
00:31:37,478 --> 00:31:39,439
- Hey.
- You're dressed for summer?

642
00:31:39,522 --> 00:31:41,274
How are you doing, lady?

643
00:31:43,735 --> 00:31:45,653
I don't know how to respond to that.

644
00:31:47,113 --> 00:31:50,158
<i>Today, we have prepared</i>
<i>a date for you to enjoy.</i>

645
00:31:50,241 --> 00:31:51,451
<i>Oh, here it comes.</i>

646
00:31:51,534 --> 00:31:53,912
<i>The women will compete against each other,</i>

647
00:31:53,995 --> 00:31:58,333
<i>and the winner will be able to invite</i>
<i>the man she's interested in.</i>

648
00:31:58,416 --> 00:32:00,585
- What kind of game?
- Beach flags?

649
00:32:01,085 --> 00:32:04,422
<i>Okay, everyone,</i>
<i>please change into your swimsuits</i>

650
00:32:04,505 --> 00:32:06,215
<i>and head down to the beach.</i>

651
00:32:08,885 --> 00:32:10,428
- <i>Wow, nice!</i>
- <i>Yeah.</i>

652
00:32:10,511 --> 00:32:12,055
<i>Okinawa!</i>

653
00:32:12,138 --> 00:32:14,057
- Look, here they come.
- Whoa.

654
00:32:14,140 --> 00:32:15,350
Nice.

655
00:32:15,934 --> 00:32:17,060
Sexy.

656
00:32:17,644 --> 00:32:19,979
<i>Oh, my! Here they come.</i>

657
00:32:35,161 --> 00:32:36,537
Looking good.

658
00:32:36,621 --> 00:32:38,331
Creepy.

659
00:32:39,082 --> 00:32:41,042
- Why do you have a bat?
- Shut your trap.

660
00:32:41,125 --> 00:32:42,627
You hear me?

661
00:32:43,920 --> 00:32:45,922
Huh?

662
00:32:47,966 --> 00:32:49,258
- It's starting.
- Yeah.

663
00:32:49,842 --> 00:32:51,511
<i>Today's competition is…</i>

664
00:32:51,594 --> 00:32:54,180
<i>- a princess-carry race.</i>
- Wow.

665
00:32:54,263 --> 00:32:55,598
- No way!
- What the heck?

666
00:32:55,682 --> 00:32:57,141
- What?
- What is that?

667
00:32:57,225 --> 00:33:00,353
<i>All of the women</i>
<i>will have to be princess-carried</i>

668
00:33:00,436 --> 00:33:02,522
<i>- by the men in this race.</i>
- <i>What's that mean?</i>

669
00:33:02,605 --> 00:33:05,692
<i>The first woman</i>
<i>to cross the finish line wins.</i>

670
00:33:05,775 --> 00:33:07,694
- <i>Sounds fun.</i>
- <i>It's a fun game.</i>

671
00:33:07,777 --> 00:33:10,697
<i>Ladies, please choose a man to carry you.</i>

672
00:33:10,780 --> 00:33:11,906
We're choosing one?

673
00:33:11,990 --> 00:33:15,243
<i>Please note,</i>
<i>the one you pick to go on a date with</i>

674
00:33:15,326 --> 00:33:17,412
<i>does not have to be the same man</i>

675
00:33:17,495 --> 00:33:19,580
<i>who princess-carried you</i>
<i>across the finish line.</i>

676
00:33:19,664 --> 00:33:21,582
This is the worst, seriously.

677
00:33:21,666 --> 00:33:24,502
So, they could choose someone
they like, or someone they trust to win.

678
00:33:24,585 --> 00:33:26,379
- I see.
- That's cruel.

679
00:33:26,462 --> 00:33:28,631
It's cruel for sure, but I like it.

680
00:33:29,132 --> 00:33:32,301
- This is exciting.
- This is about going for the win, right?

681
00:33:32,385 --> 00:33:34,554
- I go first?
- Know who you'll pick?

682
00:33:34,637 --> 00:33:36,472
"Going for the win."

683
00:33:40,184 --> 00:33:41,019
Kazuma.

684
00:33:41,102 --> 00:33:42,937
- Oh!
- Hey!

685
00:33:43,021 --> 00:33:43,896
Uh-oh!

686
00:33:43,980 --> 00:33:45,606
- Whoo!
- I'm jealous.

687
00:33:46,357 --> 00:33:48,317
Kazuma. Now, Rinrin.

688
00:33:49,777 --> 00:33:51,446
She's got such long legs.

689
00:33:51,529 --> 00:33:52,905
So long.

690
00:33:52,989 --> 00:33:54,073
Well…

691
00:33:55,616 --> 00:33:56,951
I choose Ryopi.

692
00:33:57,035 --> 00:33:59,162
- Hey.
- Gosh, such long legs!

693
00:34:00,621 --> 00:34:01,622
I choose…

694
00:34:04,459 --> 00:34:05,293
Rune.

695
00:34:05,376 --> 00:34:06,586
- Okay.
- Whoa.

696
00:34:06,669 --> 00:34:08,129
- Nice.
- Okay.

697
00:34:09,255 --> 00:34:11,382
- So, who's it gonna be?
- Oh, shit.

698
00:34:12,759 --> 00:34:13,593
Please.

699
00:34:16,596 --> 00:34:18,306
- We're going for the win, so…
- Yeah?

700
00:34:18,389 --> 00:34:19,474
…Kazuma.

701
00:34:19,557 --> 00:34:20,808
- Whoa!
- Man.

702
00:34:20,892 --> 00:34:23,061
- Double request!
- What happens now?

703
00:34:23,144 --> 00:34:25,146
No way.

704
00:34:25,229 --> 00:34:27,857
For real? Are you fighting over Kazuma?

705
00:34:27,940 --> 00:34:30,109
- Look at you, Mr. Popular.
- He's so popular.

706
00:34:30,860 --> 00:34:33,946
I had zero yesterday. That's how popular
I am right now.

707
00:34:34,030 --> 00:34:35,740
He couldn't sleep at all.

708
00:34:36,449 --> 00:34:38,493
- Kazuma, you choose.
- Wow, for real?

709
00:34:38,576 --> 00:34:41,037
- Then, Sara.
- Yeah!

710
00:34:41,120 --> 00:34:43,748
- Oh, wow.
- Thank you, please win this.

711
00:34:43,831 --> 00:34:46,292
- I hope we win.
- She said, "Please win this."

712
00:34:46,375 --> 00:34:48,294
